WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.630
- [Instructor] What were
going to do in this video

00:00:01.630 --> 00:00:04.210
is think a little bit
about place value tables

00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:07.310
and sometimes they're referred
to as place value charts.

00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:09.280
In previous videos, we've
already talked about

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:11.091
the idea of place value,

00:00:11.091 --> 00:00:14.470
and a place value table
or a place value chart

00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:17.920
is just a way to say how much we have,

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:20.240
how much value we have in each place

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:21.950
in a very, very clear way.

00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:25.667
So, here they say use the place
value chart to write 60,229.

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:31.360
And, this is the place value
table or place value chart

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:32.193
right over here.

00:00:32.193 --> 00:00:33.510
They say, enter a digit,

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:36.460
one-digit number in each box
of the place value chart.

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:37.590
So really, all they're saying is

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:39.160
how many 10 thousands do we have?

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:40.490
How many thousands?

00:00:40.490 --> 00:00:41.620
How many hundreds?

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:42.900
How many tens?

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:44.470
And, how many ones?

00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:46.740
And like always, it's always a good idea

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:49.030
to try to have a go at it
before I do it with you.

00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:49.940
So, why don't you do that?

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:51.060
Why don't you pause the video

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:52.900
and on a little piece of scratch paper

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:57.230
say how many 10 thousands are in 60,229?

00:00:57.230 --> 00:00:58.490
How many thousands are there?

00:00:58.490 --> 00:00:59.323
How many hundreds?

00:00:59.323 --> 00:01:00.156
How many tens?

00:01:00.156 --> 00:01:01.870
And, how many ones?

00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:03.826
All right, now let's do this together.

00:01:03.826 --> 00:01:08.180
So, we could start at the left
in the 10 thousands place.

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:09.520
This is the ones place.

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:11.040
This is the tens place.

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:12.500
Let me do that a little bit neater.

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:15.880
So, this is ones, tens, hundreds,

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:17.644
thousands, 10 thousands.

00:01:17.644 --> 00:01:21.290
So, we can see that we
have six 10 thousands.

00:01:21.290 --> 00:01:23.320
So, all we would do is
say, we'd put a six there.

00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:24.956
We have six 10 thousands.

00:01:24.956 --> 00:01:26.845
And then, how many thousands?

00:01:26.845 --> 00:01:29.439
Well, that would be one
place over to the right.

00:01:29.439 --> 00:01:31.040
This is interesting.

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:32.100
We can see very clearly,

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:34.960
we actually have zero thousands.

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:36.390
So, zero thousands.

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:37.223
You might say, hey.

00:01:37.223 --> 00:01:39.890
When you say this out you say 60,229.

00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:41.630
Don't we have 60 thousands?

00:01:41.630 --> 00:01:42.870
Well, you already accounted for that

00:01:42.870 --> 00:01:44.746
in the six 10 thousands.

00:01:44.746 --> 00:01:47.190
Six 10 thousands is 60,000.

00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:51.030
But just in the thousands
place, you have none.

00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:54.023
And then, we move on
to the hundreds place.

00:01:54.023 --> 00:01:57.137
You can see very clearly
we have two hundreds,

00:01:57.137 --> 00:02:00.620
and then we can go to the tens place.

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:02.040
And, I've written over it a little bit,

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:03.340
but we have two tens.

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:05.720
And then last but not least,

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:08.270
we have nine ones.

00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:09.340
And, we're done.

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:10.600
And so, the whole point of this video

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:13.080
is to just get you comfortable
with this type of format

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:15.400
with a place value table
or a place value chart,

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:16.410
and all it is,

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:18.507
is a way of really clearly writing out

00:02:18.507 --> 00:02:20.808
how much value you have in each place

00:02:20.808 --> 00:02:23.643
in a number like this.

